WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.391
Ten countries and regions on five questions:

2
00:00:03.391 --> 00:00:08.920
tax on gains, coin-to-coin swaps, exchange licences, leverage and data exchange.

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:14.726
Green means the rule is milder for an individual, yellow is ordinary, red is strict.

4
00:00:15.726 --> 00:00:21.291
Under CARF rules, exchanges collect client data and pass it to their own country's

5
00:00:21.291 --> 00:00:25.227
tax office, which forwards it to the country of residence.

6
00:00:25.227 --> 00:00:30.385
Tax offices will see 2026 trades on exchanges in the European Union, the UK,

7
00:00:30.385 --> 00:00:32.489
South Africa and Japan in 2027.

8
00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:35.272
The UAE and Singapore start a year later.

9
00:00:35.272 --> 00:00:40.158
“An exchange abroad” no longer means “the tax office will not find out”.

10
00:00:41.158 --> 00:00:43.694
The spread between countries is wide.

11
00:00:43.694 --> 00:00:49.039
In Germany, coins sold after more than a year are not taxed for an individual.

12
00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:54.453
In the UK it is 18 or 24 percent, and the first 3,000 pounds of gains are free.

13
00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:58.291
In the UAE, Singapore and Hong Kong gains are not taxed,

14
00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.552
but only for their tax residents.

15
00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:04.870
In Japan it is currently up to 55 percent on the general scale.
